  "title": "Erdős Problem #1002",
  "statement": {
    "representation": "markdown-latex",
    "text": "For any $0<\\alpha<1$, let $ f(\\alpha,n)=\\frac{1}{\\log n}\\sum_{1\\leq k\\leq n}(\\tfrac{1}{2}-\\{ \\alpha k\\}). $ Does $f(\\alpha,n)$ have an asymptotic distribution function?\nIn other words, is there a non-decreasing function $g$ such that $g(-\\infty)=0$, $g(\\infty)=1$,\nand $ \\lim_{n\\to \\infty}\\lvert \\{ \\alpha\\in (0,1): f(\\alpha,n)\\leq c\\}\\rvert=g(c)? $ ",
